herolte: libheroapp (the uncaught exception text) also goes into assetsd (0430)

assetsd aborts on an uncaught Objective-C exception (Photos, Safari photo picker) and launchd drops its stderr; the plist redirection of hero-run left the file empty (min51b), so the insertion that already puts libheroapp into applications now covers the daemon whose path ends in /assetsd. Needs the library in the drop zone, as for the applications.

--- a/bsd/dev/herolte_gl.c
+++ b/bsd/dev/herolte_gl.c
@@ -169,6 +169,14 @@
 			poster = poster || strncmp(p, "Poster", 6) == 0;
 		}
 		in_applications = appex && poster;
+		/*
+		 * 0430: assetsd (the photo library's daemon) aborts on an uncaught exception whose text never reached the log
+		 * (launchd keeps its stderr; min50-min51); libheroapp's last words say it. Same insertion as for the applications.
+		 */
+		size_t pl = strlen(path);
+		if (pl >= 8 && strcmp(path + pl - 8, "/assetsd") == 0) {
+			in_applications = true;
+		}
 	}
 	if (in_applications && max >= 1) {
 		vnode_t appvp = NULLVP;
